gbone wrote:
> Does anyone have a good strategy for playing the wizard class?  I've tried
> just spellcasting and using non-metalic armour but it seems that creatures
> just seem to hit way to often.  My recent stragety seems to more effective,
> which is to just play like a fighter class and load up on all types of
> armour.  Does any have any hints or tips on playing this class?

Firstly, playing (and dying as) wizards really improved my game when I 
finally started producing ascendable characters last year.
I eventually YAFAPed a Val (named Trogdrix) in April 2003, and YAAPed a 
Wiz (named Mupp) 2 months later.

It's a great class, in that you won't get away with stuff (bad habits) 
that will get you killed anyway, just deeper into the dungeon.
As I see it, dying as a Wiz on lvl 5 is often caused by the same 
behaviour that would have killed a Val on lvl 10 anyway.


Anyway, as to tips:

!!!SPOILER WARNING!!!

- Start wielding dagger/athame straight away. Sacrifice to get Magicbane 
early, enchant to +2.
- Don't descend too quickly. Until around Sokoban, if my character level 
is lower than the Dlvl, I feel like I'm mocking the RNG.
- Improve your strategies on ranged attacks (magic or otherwise) and pet 
keeping.
- #engrave Elbereth (I try not to, since I usually screwed up if I find 
myself in a situation where I need to engrave... but that's a matter of 
playing style - a lot of highly skilled players engrave the time).
- Lastly: don't give up on wizards! You'll die a lot, but you'll also 
learn quickly.

Every time you die, take a moment and make notes (mental or otherwise) 
on how you could have prevented it. Be honest to yourself.

I'm sure this thread will provide you with lots of useful advice, but in 
the end, the best way to actually remember to (e.g.) keep a fire source 
handy at all times - is to have that personal, painful encounter with a 
green slime; and curse and cry and promise yourself never to die like 
that again :)

Good luck!

